# Portfolio Coding Standards

## Must Follow
- No inline styles in JSX/TSX. Use style files only.
- Strict TypeScript only. Do not use `any`, unsafe casts, or `@ts-ignore` unless explicitly approved.
- Never disable lint rules (`eslint-disable`, `eslint-disable-next-line`, etc.).

## Component Folder Structure
- Every component must live in its own folder named after the component.
- Each component folder must include:
  - `index.tsx` for component markup/logic
  - `styles` file for that component styles (for example `styles.css`)
  - `consts` file for static values (for example `consts.ts`)
- Keep constants out of `index.tsx` when they are reusable/static config.

## General Standards
- Use React function components with clear, typed props.
- Prefer semantic HTML (`header`, `main`, `section`, `footer`) where relevant.
- Keep accessibility basics: meaningful `alt`, `label`, `aria-label`, and button types.
- After substantial edits, run lint and fix introduced issues.
